<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.layer.reads ~ survey wiki residency and layer access

With no `recipe`, the read surveys the catalog, activation and vessel residency. With a `recipe`, it names each layer the wiki composes and whether this session's face reads and writes it, and `working` names the layer a put lands in. `target` visits another lit face's read view.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///engine.layer.reads", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ recipe · target

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`recipe` params=`takes/word ~ the wiki (default names the worn face's daemon wiki)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`target` params=`takes/word ~ another lit face to visit (h1, or a pet name)`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! act lar:///engine.layer.reads

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/seat spells/[[act lar:///engine.layer.reads]] ~ the seat runs it in its own process`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

